  "proof_scope": "In progress. R1726 proves actual padded field reading, self-contained pair parsing, and a reusable whole-batch normalizer. PreparedPair prepares and erases its width template from the short dimension; two output fields preserve their values and gain fixed zero padding. NormalizedBatch is one6-tape5-symbol program with small+2*pad+197states, independent of dimension and record count. It reads a pair, appends both normalized fields, physically erases both temporary fields, and repeats; STOP is consumed and copied once. Arbitrary input prefix/suffix and output prefix, all absolute head positions, and framed native calls are proved. Source survives;template and both field tapes return blank. A batch of R pairs costs R*(80*ell+37*small+22*pad+84)+20*ell+7*small+31. With pad=Cmax-small,this is at most(R+1)*(80*ell+37*Cmax+84). A proved dense record-count bound and bit-size comparison give at most(74*Cmax+648)*inputLength(N) per map for short normalized dimension and N>=1. Fourteen modules/93theorems added;fullbuild9297jobs,1692audited declarations,standard axioms only. Finite-family normalization/raw-generation composition and canonical processing remain. Three of six families complete.",
